  "id": "funnel_pp_tau_zero_matches_p",
  "reference": "pp funnel on a sample with no evidence of over-dispersion (phi-hat = 0.007718 < (K-1)/K): tau-hat = 0 and the limits are exactly the p funnel's exact binomial limits (ucl[0] = 0.287292 at n = 40). Cross-checked against an independent numpy + scipy.stats implementation of the whole chain (center line, Pearson residuals, winsorizing, method-of-moments tau^2, and the interpolated quantile of scipy's distribution) to ~1e-11. Upper contours sit at the exact one-sided test's boundary, one count beyond the interpolated quantile, so a point is beyond either line exactly when its exact p-value is below that line's tail probability (docs/methods.md \u00a74.1).",
